## Why This Is Asked
Reasoning about dynamic graphs with batch updates and maintaining a topological order is common in build systems and streaming pipelines; it tests both algorithmic design and practical data-structure choices.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic topological ordering
- Order-maintenance data structures
- Batch update amortization
- Localized reordering vs global rebuild

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch
class DynTopo {
  // ... maintains pos[] and a structure for order queries
  updateBatch(edges) {
    for (const [u,v] of edges) {
      if (pos[u] < pos[v]) continue;
      relocateAffected(u,v);
    }
  }
}
```

